**Overview**
 Groupe Dynamite Inc. (GDI) is a Montréal\-based, public company of integrated omni\-channel brands, designing and distributing accessible, trend\-forward fashion for women since 1975\.




 Our mission of "Empowering YOU to be YOU, one outfit at a time" is brought to life through the GARAGE and DYNAMITE banners and represents the consumer\-centric core of GDI's long\-standing success as a leading retailer in North America.




 Today, GDI operates nearly 300 stores across Canada and the United States, as well as shoppable brand experiences at Garageclothing.com and Dynamiteclothing.com.




**Job Summary**
 We see our team as an R\&D startup embedded within a larger organization. Our environment is dynamic, fuelled by constant brainstorming, technical discussions, and a love for “hacking.” Our strength lies in the diverse technical backgrounds and cultures of our team members, which propels us through our daily work.




 What truly distinguishes us is the tangible impact of our developments. Our models are deployed directly into production, significantly enhancing efficiency and fostering innovation for both our in\-store and Head Office teams. These models are presented through internal tools and directly to customers via our E\-commerce platform.




 As a member of the Data Science team, you will play a crucial role in leading, building, and advancing our demand forecasting, recommendation engines, and GenAI solutions. You will also be instrumental in establishing data science best practices across the organization.




**Main Responsibilities**
* Design and build advanced data models and scalable pipelines for production use
* Collaborate with data scientists and engineers to solve real business problems using structured and unstructured data in the cloud;
* Write efficient, high\-quality code to support Groupe Dynamite’s cloud\-based solutions;
* Develop and deploy solutions using AWS, GCP, or Snowflake;
* Build and manage end\-to\-end ML pipelines, from data prep to training, deployment, and monitoring;
* Review code and models, support MLOps practices, and help maintain strong technical standards;
* Prototype new approaches in GenAI, forecasting, and recommender systems;
* Architect, implement, and deploy advanced data models and scalable data pipelines in production.


**Qualifications**
* Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field;
* 5\+ years of experience in a similar role, with a strong track record of delivering impact in production environments;
* Strong coding skills in Python and PySpark, with 5\+ years of hands\-on experience;
* Solid experience with both relational and NoSQL databases;
* Comfortable writing efficient queries for large structured and unstructured datasets;
* Hands\-on experience building data pipelines in distributed/cloud environments;
* Experience in data science and data analytics, including statistical analysis, predictive modelling, and model evaluation;
* Practical experience with machine learning and MLOps;
* Well\-versed in modern cloud technologies, such as Lambda functions and Glue Jobs in AWS and cloud functions in GCP;
* Strong analytical problem\-solving, and critical thinking skills, attention to detail, and creativity;
* Ability to work effectively both independently and within a team;
* Strong communication skills and the ability to present technical content to non\-technical audiences.


 At GDI, You Will Be Part Of a Growing Organization That Understands The Importance Of Investing In People And Offers You




* A comprehensive compensation package that includes performance\-driven bonuses;
* A group retirement savings program with employer matching;
* Flexible group insurance with personalized coverage that meets your needs;
* An employee discount at Garage and Dynamite;
* Exclusive private sample sales;
* A flexible vacation policy;
* And more!


 GDI has been repeatedly voted one of Montréal’s Top Employers and one of Canada’s Top Employers for Young People.




**Our promise…**
 No day will be like the last—we aim to be better today than we were yesterday. We are committed to employment equity.




 Candidates that are retained will be called for an interview.

* Permanent, Full\-time opportunity (37\.5 hours per week)
* Convenient Docklands Location – 727 Collins St
* Base salary of $80,166


 We are seeking a talented
 **Data Scientist** 
 to join our
 **JLT** 
 team at
 **Marsh.** 
 This role will be based in the
 **Melbourne** 
 office. This is a hybrid role that has a requirement of working at least three days a week in the office.




 As a
 **Data Scientist** 
 you will develop BI and Data models with emphasis on QlikView data models and dashboards to support internal and external client needs. The role requires complete comprehension of enterprise data models and utilization of both relational and dimensional data sources.




**We will count on you to:**
* Perform detailed analysis of source systems and source system data and model that data in QlikView;
* Design, develop, and test QlikView scripts to import data from source systems and test QlikView dashboards to meet customer requirements;
* Interpret written business requirements and technical specification documents;
* Create and maintain technical design documentation;
* Perform quality coding to business and technical specifications;
* Work directly with business units to define and prototype QlikView Applications;
* Extracting, transforming and loading data from multiple sources into QlikView applications Monitoring and maintenance of all components that make up the Data Warehouse and Business Intelligence infrastructure;
* Act as evangelist for BI benefits across the organization; promote BI usage to relevant departments;
* Responsible for demonstrating software to internal users;
* Participate in design meetings;
* Create standards and prototypes;
* Prepare and maintain relevant technical documentation.


**What you need to have:**
* Experience in developing / architecting BI Solutions supporting financial, sales and performance reporting;
* Experience in sourcing data from disparate systems with a good understanding of their Data Models;
* Hands\-on professional with thorough knowledge of scripting, data source integration and advanced GUI development in QlikView;
* Full understanding of the processes of data quality, data cleansing and data transformation Ability to write complicated yet efficient SQL queries and stored procedures;
* Strong knowledge on QlikView server architecture and building qvd’s and qvw’s applying business rules and data validations;
* Experience in end\-to\-end implementation of Business Intelligence (BI) projects, especially in scorecards, KPIs, reports \& dashboards
* Knowledge of formal database architecture and design;
* Tertiary education with a degree in computer science, information technology, information systems, or a related discipline;
* Detail\-oriented with strong organizational, analytical and communication skills;
* Results\-driven with the ability to take initiatives, handle multiple tasks and shifting priorities and meet deadlines;
* Excellent problem solving skills, logical process thinking and end\-to\-end system concepts
* Thinks clearly and calmly under pressure;
* Places emphasis on client satisfaction;
* Promotes the mission and shared values of JLT and Marsh;
* Excellent interpersonal and organisational skills with a strong ability to articulate and communicate ideas, work requirements and performance based matters in an empathetic manner;
* Self\-motivated and results driven with a consultative approach.


**Why join our team:**
* We help you be your best through professional development opportunities, interesting work and supportive leaders.
* We foster a vibrant and inclusive culture where you can work with talented colleagues to create new solutions and have impact for colleagues, clients and communities.
* Our scale enables us to provide a range of career opportunities, as well as benefits and rewards to enhance your well\-being.


**How to Apply:**
 Follow the link to apply. Applications will be open from
 **03 September** 
 to
 **01 October.**
***Applications will only be considered from candidates who have the appropriate approval to work in Australia. Successful applicants will be required to complete a Criminal \& Bankruptcy check prior to commencement of employment.***
**About Marsh**
 Marsh, a business of Marsh McLennan (NYSE: MMC), is the world’s top insurance broker and risk advisor. Marsh McLennan is a global leader in risk, strategy and people, advising clients in 130 countries across four businesses: Marsh, Guy Carpenter, Mercer and Oliver Wyman. With annual revenue of $24 billion and more than 90,000 colleagues, Marsh McLennan helps build the confidence to thrive through the power of perspective. For more information, visit marsh.com, or follow on LinkedIn and X.




 Marsh McLennan is committed to creating a diverse, inclusive and flexible work environment. We aim to attract and retain the best people and embrace diversity of age, background, disability, ethnic origin, family duties, gender orientation or expression, marital status, nationality, parental status, personal or social status, political affiliation, race, religion and beliefs, sex/gender, sexual orientation or expression, skin color, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.




 Marsh McLennan is committed to hybrid work, which includes the flexibility of working remotely and the collaboration, connections and professional development benefits of working together in the office. All Marsh McLennan colleagues are expected to be in their local office or working onsite with clients at least three days per week. Office\-based teams will identify at least one “anchor day” per week on which their full team will be together in person.




**R\_319867**

**About Deep Origin**  

Deep Origin is a biotechnology company accelerating drug discovery through AI\-powered tools. Our platforms simplify R\&D, simulate biology, and empower scientists to solve diseases and extend human healthspan through software solutions and partnerships. We integrate advanced computational methods with experimental data to model biological systems at scale.

**Role Description:**  

We are seeking a skilled Data Scientist with expertise in quantitative pharmacokinetics, parameter estimation, and metabolic modeling. You need to develop hybrid computational frameworks that combine ordinary differential equation\-based (ODE\-based) simulations with machine learning methods to predict metabolic parameters, distribution profiles, and biotransformation outcomes.


This is a highly interdisciplinary role requiring strong mathematical modeling skills, statistical acumen, and experience integrating diverse datasets into robust predictive models. Combining expertise in systems pharmacology, machine learning, and data\-driven modeling, you will develop hybrid approaches that unite mechanistic simulations with AI\-driven predictions, powering Deep Origin’s next\-generation AI\-powered metabolism and pharmacokinetic simulation platform.



Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time.

**Requirements**

* PhD (0\-2 years) or MS (2\-5 years) of relevant experience in Systems Biology, Computational Pharmacology, Applied Mathematics, or related field;
* Strong background in ODE/PDE modeling, numerical simulation, and parameter estimation;
* Experience with pharmacokinetic model development;
* Proficiency in Python;
* Basic understanding of drug metabolism and pharmacokinetics (DMPK) concepts;
* Strong statistical analysis skills and experience with Bayesian or frequentist inference methods;
* Ability to critically analyze data and translate findings into actionable predictions and computational models;
* Collaborative mindset, comfortable working in both autonomous and team\-based settings;
Adaptability to thrive in a fast\-paced, deadline\-driven environment.  
* 

**Nice to have:**

Familiarity with multi\-scale modeling (molecular tissue* organism);
* Exposure to machine learning for parameter prediction or model reduction;
* Prior pharmaceutical or biotech industry experience.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* Develop and calibrate ODE\-based models for drug metabolism and distribution;
* Predict key metabolic and pharmacokinetic parameters (e.g., Vmax, Km);
* Model Phase I and Phase II metabolic networks at the systems level;
* Simulate compound distribution inside a defined compartment;
* Apply statistical inference and optimization techniques to fit models to experimental and clinical data;
* Integrate genetic polymorphism data to simulate inter\-individual variability in metabolism;
* Engage with colleagues across disciplines to iteratively develop and strengthen models.

**Why Join Us?**

* Work on impactful problems at the frontier of AI \+ chemistry \+ biology;
* Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams of scientists;
* Shape next\-generation tools for predictive drug discovery.

### **Who we are**


ZYTLYN Technologies empowers companies across the $11 trillion travel industry to shape the future with predictive AI solutions that augment commercial planning, sales, marketing, retailing and operations. We work with some of the largest travel brands in the world, and our vision is to answer highly detailed and granular questions about the future of travel, such as demand, supply, market fluctuations and pricing. Our core focus is on airlines, airports, travel agencies, destinations, tourism boards, hotels, car rentals, travel retailers, and luxury brands.

### **Who we are looking for**


We’re looking for a versatile and hands\-on Growth \& Marketing Executive to take the lead on our content marketing and storytelling — writing exceptional content, creating professional, high\-impact content and materials that showcase our vision, products, and customer success. You’ll develop a wide range of lead magnets, such as blog posts/articles, market trends insights/commentary, press releases, videos, case studies, tutorials, website updates, digital campaign assets, and physical marketing collateral for events and trade shows\- with direction and input from the CEO and the wider team. A key part of your work will be creating lead magnets designed to capture qualified leads and engage decision\-makers.


Alongside marketing, you will also work on growth, specifically through personalised sales development: identifying and reaching out to prospects (e.g. phone, email, LinkedIn), engaging them through various channels, and nurturing them until demo stage. You’ll support enterprise deal cycles, while ensuring sales pipeline discipline and consistent customer engagement. This is an ideal role for someone who loves combining creative marketing execution, lead magnet creation, and commercial hustle, and who thrives in a startup environment where you can contribute to the foundation of our growth engine.

### **Location / Contract type**

* Geneva, Switzerland Office/Hybrid, or;
* Full remote contractor (GMT\+1 to GMT\+4\).

### **Our culture**


We have a culture that focuses on empowering people, with team members working in our HQ (Geneva, Switzerland), and all across Europe (e.g. France, Spain, Italy, Poland, UK). We believe a diverse team creates better outcomes and fosters a better environment for learning and growth. We put a lot of emphasis on communication, listening, efficient processes and trusting our team. We rely on each other, and work together to achieve our common goals. We believe in working smart, with strong focus and intensity, tackling every challenge as a team.

### **Your work**

* Develop compelling content marketing, sales, and lead magnet branded materials such as blogs/articles, data/trend insight reports, press releases, videos, case studies, tutorials, website updates, sales campaign assets, product decks, and physical marketing collateral for events and trade shows;
* Capture, edit, and produce video content, such as customer success stories, explainer videos, demo walkthroughs, short clips, to boost engagement and visibility;
* Manage website, blog, LinkedIn, and newsletter updates;
* Tailor messaging for executives, commercial and technical leaders across the travel industry;
* Generate and qualify leads via manual, highly personalised and targeted outreach (e.g. LinkedIn, email, phone);
* Nurture leads persistently until demo stage; support engagement post\-demo until deal closure;
* Contribute to CRM hygiene (Pipedrive, Apollo, LinkedIn Sales Navigator), and pipeline discipline;
* Support sales with enterprise deal cycles, including procurement, licensing, and contracting.

**Requirements**

### **Basic requirements**

* 4\+ years of content marketing experience in b2b;
* Exceptional writing skills — able to produce both high\-quality long\-form content, and sharp, persuasive copy (ads, email campaigns, landing pages) in superb English;
* Experience using content creation tools (e.g. Jasper, ChatGPT);
* Experience using design and asset creation tools (e.g. PowerPoint, Canva, Figma, Visme, Adobe Creative Cloud);
* Experience using video creation and editing tools (e.g. Synthesia, Riverside, Google Vids);
* 2\+ years of B2B sales or sales development experience;
* Proven track record in lead generation, sales pipeline building, and opportunity creation;
* Familiar with CRM and sales tools (Apollo, Hubspot, LinkedIn Sales Navigator);
* Resourceful self\-starter, comfortable with ambiguity and shifting priorities in a startup;
* Highly organised, disciplined, and detail\-oriented;
* Excellent English communication skills — verbal, written, and executive presence;

### **Bonus points**

* Existing strong relationships with decision makers across travel, airlines, airports, OTAs, and tourism boards;
* Experience positioning b2b data analytics/AI products;
* Experience supporting enterprise deal cycles (procurement, licensing, multi\-year contracts);
* Experience designing and managing paid ad campaigns (LinkedIn Ads, Google Ads) to drive targeted B2B awareness and lead generation.

**Benefits**

### **What we offer**

* Join a team of exceptional talent — At ZYTLYN, we hire thoughtfully and selectively, bringing together a small, focused team of high performers. We believe that a lean and empowered team moves faster, builds smarter, and achieves more. You’ll collaborate with driven colleagues who value efficiency, ownership, and impact.
* Swiss employment contract based in Geneva/hybrid, or full remote b2b contract option.
* Competitive salary\- adjusted for experience and market benchmarks.
* Eligible for equity in a well\-capitalised Series A startup with high growth potential, bringing together engineers, data scientists, product builders, marketers, and commercial industry experts\- all passionate about solving tough problems with global impact.
